  "summary_en": "First draft of Iraq's National AI Policy from the Prime Minister's Office. It sets a vision of regional AI leadership and six work axes: capacity building, R&D and entrepreneurship, data and infrastructure, sectoral adoption, international cooperation, and enabling environment. It stresses incentives, an ethics charter and human oversight. It contains no robotics-specific provisions.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Vision of Iraq as a leading regional AI hub through a safe, fair, sustainable digital environment",
   "Six work axes: capacity, R&D/innovation, data and infrastructure, sectoral adoption, cooperation, enabling environment",
   "Calls for an ethics charter, data protection regulations and data classification/sharing guidance",
   "Human oversight stressed: full responsibility rests on human operators, not the machine",
   "Investment incentives, tax exemptions for AI hardware/software imports, and annual committee review of the policy"
